Third-party work
----------------

A skills/<name> folder whose name is also listed in upstream/sources.json is
a modified copy of that upstream skill. Upstream text in it stays under the
upstream license named there. tstack by Theo Browne
(https://github.com/t3dotgg/tstack) is MIT licensed, included as
upstream/LICENSE-tstack.

upstream/pstack-codex/codex.md draws on pstack-claude by Michael Denyer, with Lauren Tan
(https://github.com/michael-denyer/pstack-claude), MIT licensed. Its license
text is included as upstream/pstack-codex/LICENSE-pstack-claude.

upstream/overlays/untangle-codebase/ is laid over untangle-codebase
(https://github.com/caldoai/skills) and keeps that project's license, included
there.

Everything listed in upstream/sources.json is pinned, not copied, and is
installed from its own source under its own license.
